# Example workbook

## Let's define a factorial

j(define (fact n) 
  (if (= n 1)
    1
    (* n (fact (- n 1)))))

## Let's try run it

Factorial of 4 is 24:

j(fact 4)

Factorial of 10 is going to be giant!

j(fact 10)

## Importing maths

j(import "maths")

Let's use this to find the square root of 16

j(maths/sqrt 16)

I've got lots of mysterious circles to contend with, let's write a helper
function for them

j(define (circle-area r) 
  (* r r maths/pi))

Great.  Let's find the area of a circle!

j(circle-area 10)

j(circle-area 100)

j(circle-area 56)
